      "description": "Uses count_in_box_at_least(kind='block', object='white_wool', min_count=5) because this is a build/place task — the player must place white wool blocks to form a road. The detection box covers x=-10 to x=2, y=0, z=-10 to z=10 (spawn-relative), which intentionally EXCLUDES x=3-5 where the pre-existing wool pile sits (9 blocks at x=3-5, z=3-5 plus 1 at x=4,y=1,z=4). This ensures only newly player-placed blocks are counted. The box is generous (±10 XZ) to allow the player to build the road anywhere in the western/central portion of the platform. Min_count=5 represents a minimal but recognizable road segment.",
